<title>USA: Pikeville CEO resigns, Burlin Coleman named interim.</title>
<headline>Pikeville CEO resigns, Burlin Coleman named interim.</headline>
<dateline>PIKEVILLE, Ky. 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pikeville National Corp said on Friday that Chairman Burlin Coleman will assume the positions of president and chief executive, replacing Terry Coleman, who has resigned.</p>
<p>Pikeville said Terry Coleman left the firm effective Nov. 1, to pursue other personal opportunities.</p>
<p>Burlin Coleman will serve until a successor is named, the company said. He retired as the chief executive officer on Dec. 31, 1994, but continued to serve as the board's chairman.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
